{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1495131-strange-shades-mekhet-supplement-overview","id":1495131,"title":"Strange Shades: Mekhet, supplement overview.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-17T12:12:18-07:00","id":1495131,"title":"Strange Shades: Mekhet, supplement overview.","content":"Video link:<br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/dt_K53M5GfA\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/dt_K53M5GfA</a> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Connected/IT</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Description - Answering the question of what if a hacker could use their blood to control machines.</li> <li>Disciplines - Gain Interface</li> <li>Bloodline Gift - Interface. A Discipline which allows Connected to:<ul><li>Command electronic devices with just their voice.</li> <li>Repair and turn electronic devices into a temporary Ghoul-like entities.</li> <li>Curse a target to have electronics fail when they use them.</li> <li>Cause electronics to go haywire nearby them and attack people.</li> <li>User creates a Domain where they can know every electronic device within the domain and can teleport via Wi-fi.</li> </ul></li> <li>Bloodline Curse - Anonymous Curse. The Connected get Distracted in large crowds of people.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Csalad/Stone Sires</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Description - City dwelling vampires who use Blood Sorcery to manipulate their territory and those within it.</li> <li>Disciplines - Gain Lithopedia</li> <li>Bloodline Gift - Lithopedia, is Blood Sorcerery that affects the user\u2019s territory or those within the their territory.<ul><li>Extend Predatory Aura over the territory and sense non-Obfuscated trespassers in their territory.</li> <li>Can sense general emotional state of territory and add Lithopedia dots to Empathy rolls inside territory.</li> </ul></li> <li>Bloodline Curse - Civic Curse. Resting anywhere, but their personal territory causes them to become Lethargic.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m not sure if I\u2019d play one of these, but </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kuufukuji/Celibates</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Description - Vampires who can go without feeding for longer than others through fasting techniques.</li> <li>Disciplines - Gain Resilience</li> <li>Bloodline Gift - Shihai merit. By abstaining from feeding the user gains bonus like:<ul><li>Being able to identify, calm, or worsen Frenzy.</li> <li>Resist Frenzy via harming ones\u2019 self.</li> <li>Damage themself to increase their Physical attributes.</li> <li>Can more easily Lash Out to stop another Frenzying.</li> <li>Replace Vitae with Temptation for powering abilities.</li> </ul></li> <li>Bloodline Curse - Ascetic Curse. Drinking too much Vitae in a night can turn them Bestial till they abstain.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Leandros/Heartbreakers</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Description - Vampires who get attached to a single mortal to the extent that it is toxic to the mortal.</li> <li>Disciplines - Replace Celerity with Majesty and Vigor.</li> <li>Bloodline Gift - New Devotions<ul><li>Can increase their Impression to Perfect.</li> <li>Can gain temporary resistance to Sunlight.</li> <li>Appear to be a victim\u2019s perfect soul mate.</li> <li>Become Soulmates with a Mortal to gain bonuses, but at the cost of damaging the Mortal\u2019s relationship with friends and family.</li> </ul></li> <li>Bloodline Curse - Infatuated Curse. If they feed from a victim they risk that victim becoming the only vessel they can get Vitae from. If this hasn\u2019t happened they have the Invitation Bane.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mnemosyne/Mind-Thieves</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Description - Vampires who can steal memories from feeding.</li> <li>Disciplines - Gain Dominate.</li> <li>Bloodline Gift - Eidetic Memory merit. Additionally new Devotions such as:<ul><li>Bottle memories and emotions.</li> <li>Resist mind manipulation, such as via Alchohal and Obfuscate, though Clash of Wills still applies.</li> <li>Steal memories from victims they feed from.</li> <li>Restore memories from victims they feed from.</li> </ul></li> <li>Bloodline Curse - Gestalt Curse. When Feeding they risk incorporating their victim\u2019s memory into their own.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Norvegi/Knives</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Description - Vampires that can manifest spikes of blood from their flesh and turn their ghouls into monsters.</li> <li>Disciplines - Replace Obfuscate with Protean and Vigor</li> <li>Bloodline Gift - Bloodworking. New alien-like Protean Aspects and New Devotions:<ul><li>Turn a Ghoul into a Blodtrells monster, with body modification from the user\u2019s Protean Dots.</li> <li>Fire razorsharp darts of Vitae from their bodies.</li> <li>Explode crystalized vitae from their body.</li> <li>Can feed from victims via hairs on their skin instead of via fangs.</li> </ul></li> <li>Bloodline Curse - Curse of Glamr. Their skin appears to have something writhing underneath. If a Novegi Neonate hasn\u2019t dropped to Humanity 6, they start with the Fangless bane.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Qedesha/Parents</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Description - Vampires that are helicopter parents to their touchstones.</li> <li>Disciplines - Gain Majesty.</li> <li>Bloodline Gift - Embrocation. The Qedesha anoints multiple people with blood forming a mystical relationship with them.<ul><li>All of the user\u2019s Anointed are treated as 1 Touchstone.</li> <li>Can use Auspex and Majesty on them from a vast distance.</li> <li>Sense their health, injures, and current level of fear.</li> <li>Take on the wounds of an Anointed to heal them.</li> <li>Transfer Willpower to Anointed.</li> </ul></li> <li>Bloodline Curse - Fretful Curse. Must defend a touchstone or an Anoited after a few nights or become Guilty.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}